 "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 382034, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LvXzNoxDQ3LPZnqXKLzT3a", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 382034, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LvXzNoxDQ3LPZnqXKLzT3a", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 386881, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` said in its own comment that it used banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why the test failed: `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 in the security advisory system, but it isn't there. It's probably an internal finance ticket, and the fix doesn't depend on it.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files and the advisory.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SnvAXaoQNMyLzUnFdesH8A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Wm6JdiW4G4yJXXDMz